A||||1||Orlando||5spd Transmission Leak
Z||000000||Orlando||08-18-99||06:29 PM||||Has anyone ever had a 5 speed transmission that leaked? My 88 is leaking from the transmission joint. The guy I've taken it too for some other repairs says to just live with the leak, the car's not worth it. After I beat the crap out of him for insulting my baby (and paying him for some repairs, of which he did a fine job), I think I may take it to a transmission shop so I can get an estimate. Anyone?
Z||000001||batboy||08-18-99||07:20 PM||||It's probably leaking at the tranny seal where the axle (the half shaft with the CV joints on it) goes into the transmission. If you know how to replace CV joints, then it's not too hard. You have to completely remove the axle, pry the old seal out and carefully put the new one back in. There may be some wear on the axle or bearings to cause the seal to go out, so I'd check everything out closely. My guess is that your mechanic either don't know how to do the seal replacement or didn't want to do it. If you are farming out the work, take it to a driveline shop or a transmission repair shop. Hopefully they will know what to do if you tell them it's similar to doing the same job on a Chevy Citation or other GM FWD car.
